 ## [Unreleased]
 
+- **Keep neighboring code during import cleanup.** Removing an unused import preserves other statements, used imports and comments sharing its line. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
+- **Optimize PHP imports in one reviewed operation.** Workbench can remove unused imports and sort surviving standalone import blocks together, with one review and one Undo step. Source changes require a fresh request. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
+- **Report incomplete workspace indexes honestly.** Unreadable PHP files leave the index partial, and single-file sessions do not claim a complete project scan. Reference lookup retains its fallback while analysis is incomplete. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
+
 - **Check return statements against their native declaration.** Nullable PHPDoc accepts an implicit null return when no native hint is present. Native `mixed`, `void` and `never` retain PHP’s return-statement rules while supported PHPDoc refinements continue to check returned values. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
 
 - **Keep configured Storage adapters precise.** Completion, hover and navigation recognize adapter methods supplied by custom drivers even when their service provider stays closed. Unresolved drivers and ordinary filesystem contracts retain their declared limits. Contributed by PHP Workbench downstream.
